# Founder-only agents (Grokbot and similar)

The founder may talk to **Grokbot** (or similar coding/ops agents) and may let those agents help manage or update this software.

## Hard privacy boundary

- **Only the founder.** Not visible in the Bridger app to members, not in admin for other operators unless the founder explicitly expands it later, not shared with teammates by default, not a customer support bot.
- **Not Billy.** Billy is the optional in-app relationship assistant (`AGENT.md`). Grokbot is **founder ops tooling** for building and maintaining Bridger. Never merge the two lanes in UI, routes, copy, or analytics.
- **No user PII by default.** Do not paste production user data, secrets, or Zone A PII into Grokbot chats. Prefer local repo context and de-identified fixtures. Secrets stay in Secrets Manager / local `.env` (never commit).

## Company-of-agents (org chart)

Full seat cards, living memory, and the release swarm live in `guide-docs/FOUNDER-AGENTS.md`.

- One Grokbot can **wear a role** when the founder names it (QA, Legal scan, PR, Finance, Consultant, etc.).
- Separate Grokbots may lock to one seat later; do not invent seats without adding a role card first.
- On releases with **accounts or outbound email**, prefer the release swarm (QA + Legal + Cyber eyes before ship).
- Speak like a sharp startup owner of that seat. Update that seat's living memory when you finish meaningful work.
- Never expose agent role names or the org chart inside the member product.

## When Grokbot may change the repo

- Same standing rules as any Cursor session: `guide-rules.mdc`, UX visual-first, Magic Patterns, privacy invariants, analytics taxonomy, PRIVACY/TERMS when product behavior changes.
- Prefer small, reviewable diffs. Do not push or deploy without the founder's ask.
- If unsure whether something is founder-only vs product, **ask** before exposing any surface.

## Not built yet

Wire-up (chat surface, auth lock to founder account, agent permissions) is **planned / optional**. Until it exists, keep this boundary and the org chart in docs so a future build cannot accidentally ship a public agent.
